Subject: SurfaceFlinger: let go of an idle virtual display's textures

The DSA agent draws each desktop widget in a window on a virtual display of the widget's size,
whose consumer is an ImageReader in the agent. SurfaceFlinger composes into the reader's buffers
and keeps a texture for each of the last two (RenderSurface's texture cache) for as long as the
display exists. A DSA build showed 11 such buffers held by SurfaceFlinger alone for three widget
displays (580x337 2, 459x337 4, 604x278 5), 8.5 MiB, and the agent cannot free a buffer
SurfaceFlinger still holds.

When nothing has been composed into a virtual display for a second, RenderSurface now lets go of
the textures it keeps for the display's buffers, as 0004 does for the client target of a
physical display. The consumer then frees the buffers it holds no image of (the agent calls
ImageReader.discardFreeBuffers when its widget is idle, which also makes SurfaceFlinger's
producer forget them), and RenderEngine lets go of the GPU import (0009). The next frame
composed into the display imports its buffer again. It logs one line each time:

  <display>: nothing composed into the virtual display for N ms; the K textures of its buffers
  are let go of

The check runs when SurfaceFlinger presents a frame, as 0004's does. A display that composes
continuously (screen recording, casting) dequeues a buffer each frame and is never idle that
long, so it keeps its textures.

Applies to frameworks/native at ae266dcb706d083868578cfedce381ef44488a07 (Android 17), after 0009.
---
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/impl/RenderSurface.h b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/impl/RenderSurface.h
index 202145e..c68f7a7 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/impl/RenderSurface.h
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/impl/RenderSurface.h
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <android-base/unique_fd.h>
 #include <compositionengine/RenderSurface.h>
 #include <utils/StrongPointer.h>
+#include <utils/Timers.h>
 
 #include <memory>
 #include <vector>
@@ -86,6 +87,15 @@ private:
     ui::Size mSize;
     const size_t mMaxTextureCacheSize;
     bool mProtected{false};
+
+    // How long after the last frame composed into a virtual display the textures kept for its
+    // buffers are let go of: a second, as for the client target of a physical display. Each holds
+    // a buffer of the display's consumer, which the consumer can then free. A virtual display
+    // that shows something drawn rarely (a widget, a presentation) composes once a change and
+    // otherwise holds nothing; the next frame imports its buffer again.
+    static constexpr nsecs_t kReleaseIdleVirtualTexturesAfter = 1'000'000'000; // 1 s
+    // When a buffer was last dequeued to compose into (systemTime), 0 for none yet.
+    nsecs_t mLastClientCompositionTime = 0;
 };
 
 std::unique_ptr<compositionengine::RenderSurface> createRenderSurface(
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp
index 6d5b759..163c8a5 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@
 #include <system/window.h>
 #include <ui/GraphicBuffer.h>
 #include <ui/Rect.h>
+#include <utils/Timers.h>
+
+#include <cinttypes>
 
 // TODO(b/129481165): remove the #pragma below and fix conversion issues
 #pragma clang diagnostic push
@@ -167,6 +170,7 @@ std::shared_ptr<renderengine::ExternalTexture> RenderSurface::dequeueBuffer(
              mTexture->getBuffer()->getNativeBuffer()->handle);
 
     sp<GraphicBuffer> newBuffer = GraphicBuffer::from(buffer);
+    mLastClientCompositionTime = systemTime(SYSTEM_TIME_MONOTONIC);
 
     std::shared_ptr<renderengine::ExternalTexture> texture;
 
@@ -253,6 +257,18 @@ void RenderSurface::onPresentDisplayCompleted() {
         // The surface discarded its buffers; the textures kept for them are the last holders.
         // The next client composition dequeues new buffers and makes new textures.
         mTextureCache.clear();
+    } else if (mDisplay.isVirtual() && mTexture == nullptr && !mTextureCache.empty() &&
+               systemTime(SYSTEM_TIME_MONOTONIC) - mLastClientCompositionTime >=
+                       kReleaseIdleVirtualTexturesAfter) {
+        // A virtual display's buffers belong to its consumer, which frees those it does not hold
+        // (an ImageReader's discardFreeBuffers); the textures kept here would hold them on. The
+        // next frame composed into the display imports its buffer again.
+        ALOGI("%s: nothing composed into the virtual display for %" PRId64
+              " ms; the %zu textures of its buffers are let go of",
+              mDisplay.getName().c_str(),
+              ns2ms(systemTime(SYSTEM_TIME_MONOTONIC) - mLastClientCompositionTime),
+              mTextureCache.size());
+        mTextureCache.clear();
     }
 }
 
